Comments and Suggestions for Authors

1. This manuscript introduces ten structural assumptions from A1 to A10,
but the current model does not fully realize them. A9 and A10 are not used
in the model, while the basin-agreement head for A3 is inactive on all
three datasets. More experiments are needed on data that can activate and
test these assumptions, otherwise the contribution should be limited to the
assumptions that are actually validated.
2. The rare-regime-safe nearest-component likelihood in this manuscript
lacks direct experimental support. Experiments under different regime
imbalance ratios should compare mixture NLL, nearest-component NLL, and
other imbalance-aware scoring methods, with more attention to the
false-positive rate of rare normal regimes.
3. The connection to industrial-IoT system remains limited, and please cite
the following important papers:[1] Chen, Ciyuan, et al. "Enhancing Link
Performance for Mobile LoRa Networks." IEEE Transactions on Mobile
Computing (2025).[2]  Xu, Zhuqing, et al. "Leveraging
imperfect-orthogonality aware scheduling for high scalability in LPWAN."
IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing 23.10 (2024): 10111-10129.
4. The regime-community design in this manuscript trains separate
representation and density models for many communities, which may introduce
much higher cost than a single global detector. More experiments are needed
to evaluate the practical cost of this design under the same hardware
setting as the main baselines.
5. The sliding windows in this manuscript are strongly correlated in time,
so ordinary resampling may underestimate the confidence interval. A
time-aware statistical test should be used on all three datasets, and the
definition of the confidence interval and p-value on WADI should be
clarified.
6. This manuscript mainly uses six static statistics from each window, so
the source of the performance gain is still unclear. Experiments with raw
sequential input and temporal or spectral information are needed to verify
whether the gain mainly comes from cross-channel density modeling or from
the current window representation.

